From 56eaabfc4dd6ad889c01eda22cd033113f9aca31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:46:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] escha: native Escha-W2 types (ESCHA2=55/ESCHA3=56) + fused
 GGML_OP_ESCHA_MM, CPU + Vulkan

Packed EschaLabs cbA code tiles as first-class serialized weight types, payload
byte-identical to the vendor checkpoint ([in/16][out/16][16K] i16 LE). One fused
op does rin-scale -> H128 -> decode-matmul -> H128 -> rout-scale -> +bias; f32
aux sidecar <base>.escha_aux loaded by a generic pass, wired arch-agnostically
through build_lora_mm (params.mdl). Decode math = the Terra-64 PTX-recovered cbA
generator (LUT on CPU, software-f16-RTE inline on Vulkan; no float-controls
dependency). Types are NOT row-separable: generic MUL_MAT and the loader
buffer-type probe reject/route accordingly. Proofs: python-golden CPU test
(nmse ~1e-13, planted-positive), test-backend-ops ESCHA_MM 54/54 Vulkan-vs-CPU
incl. real 27B shapes, structural planted-RED + revert-GREEN receipts in
lane-evidence/2026-08-20-lane-164-escha-native/.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Conflict-resolved: auto: case-label union (upstream labels kept beside ours) in ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-push-constants.h,ggml-vulkan-types.h; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_426.py)
Conflict-resolved: auto: same-point-insertion(upstream block then ours) in ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.cpp
